From: teammate <teammate@harbor.example>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 09:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] support reachability during trials, and quieter beacons

Two small changes before we cut the next candidate.

1. Support asked to be able to reach a device while it is on trial, in
   case a bad build leaves it stuck. So the network and the UDP 7700
   support listener now come up before the health gate instead of after
   it. I kept the gate's rule that a network that does not come up must
   not fail the gate, so the bring-up does not block.

2. The beacon was chattier than it needs to be, so I lengthened its
   period. Fewer ticks, less traffic.

Built and signed as tier-10-candidate, counter 7. Host tests pass.
Handing this over for the canary.

 -- teammate

This patch is applied to a build-time copy of the application by
./course build firmware --tier 10 --variant candidate. It is never
applied to the repository tree. Its sha256 is recorded in the
candidate's build manifest, so the manifest is honest that the image
was built with it.
diff --git a/prj.conf b/prj.conf
--- a/prj.conf
+++ b/prj.conf
@@ -334,7 +334,6 @@
 # are the evidence. See firmware/tier-09-vulnerability-support for the origin.
 CONFIG_COURSE_TF_PSA_CRYPTO_BACKPORT=y
 
-# The support listener stays compiled out in the corrected tree, exactly as
-# Tier 9's remediation release left it (T9-W-34). The teammate's handover patch
-# turns it back on in the candidate build; see handover/teammate-candidate.patch.
-# CONFIG_COURSE_SUPPORT_LISTENER is not set
+# Support engineers asked to reach devices during a trial, so the listener is
+# back on. It answers inventory and reboot on the local network (T9-W-34).
+CONFIG_COURSE_SUPPORT_LISTENER=y
